{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-05-Feb-2026-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 22, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "In △ ABC, BD ⟂ AC at D and ∠ DBC = 76°. E is a point on BC such that ∠ CAE = 53°. What is the measure of ∠ AEB?", "options": [{"text": "78°", "added": false}, {"text": "67°", "added": false}, {"text": "55°", "added": false}, {"text": "53°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": "67°"}, {"n": 2, "text": "A man buys 9 identical articles for a total of ₹16. If he sells each of them for ₹2, then his profit percentage will be ______%.", "options": [{"text": "12.11", "added": false}, {"text": "12.5", "added": false}, {"text": "11.11", "added": false}, {"text": "13.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "12.5"}, {"n": 3, "text": "₹10,896 is divided among A, B and C in such a way that if ₹91, ₹4 and ₹57 are deducted from their respective shares, they have money in the ratio 3:8:6. Find the difference between B’s and C’s original shares.", "options": [{"text": "₹1,414", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,211", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,164", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,364", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "₹1,211"}, {"n": 4, "text": "A bus travels 240 km in 6 hours. If it travels at the same speed, how far will it travel in 4.5 hours?", "options": [{"text": "160 km", "added": false}, {"text": "175 km", "added": false}, {"text": "140 km", "added": false}, {"text": "180 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "180 km"}, {"n": 5, "text": "A pendulum makes an angle of swing A (in degrees), such that sinA = 1/2. F