tion 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": "2 : 17"}, {"n": 20, "text": "Find the ratio between the fourth proportional of 10, 15 and 18 to the mean proportional of 9 and 4.", "options": [{"text": "7:4", "added": false}, {"text": "10:5", "added": false}, {"text": "12:9", "added": false}, {"text": "9:2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "9:2"}, {"n": 21, "text": "The cost of a washing machine is 25% less than the cost of a TV. If the cost of the washing machine increases by 30% and that of the TV decreases by 19%, then what is the percentage change in the total cost of 8 washing machines and 4 TVs?", "options": [{"text": "Decrease by 13%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increase by 10.4%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increase by 11.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decrease by 6%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": "Increase by 10.4%"}, {"n": 22, "text": "Which is the greatest number that divides 47, 59 and 74 to leave the same remainder?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "remainder-based", "key_answer": "3"}]}